
 There are many programs including Corina, Concord and Chem3D that
 can be used to convert a 2D structure file to 3D for input to BOSS or MCPRO.
 E.g., one can copy & paste a ChemDraw 2D structure into Chem3D, which immediately
 converts it to an initial 3D structure. After a quick MM2 optimization of this
 structure, one writes it out as a .mol file. 

 The freeware WebLab ViewerLite from MSI also can
 take an ISIS or ChemDraw 2D structure to 3D and write it out as a .mol
 file. Then one can use the xMOLZ script to convert the .mol file to a
 BOSS or MCPRO .z Z-matrix file.

